  "body": "Create the pure-Rust crate `crates/gcode` (`camcraft-gcode`) beside `crates/post`.\nIt parses RS-274/NGC (NISTIR 6556) and ISO 6983 3-axis milling programs into `cl::Toolpath` sections (`crates/cl/src/cl/path.rs`) and a 1-based line map.\n\n## Scope\n- Depend only on `camcraft-cl`, `camcraft-geometry`, and `thiserror` (no `boa_engine`, no `flecs_ecs`, no `camcraft-post` dependency).\n- Record the new `camcraft-cl` and `camcraft-geometry` crate edges in `docs/decisions/` per `AGENTS.md`.\n- Accept dialect configuration and optional machine reference positions from the caller.\n- Track modal groups: motion (`G0`, `G1`, `G2`, `G3`, `G80`), plane (`G17`, `G18`, `G19`), distance (`G90`, `G91`), arc center (`G90.1`, `G91.1`), feed mode (`G94`), units (`G20`, `G21`), length offset (`G43 H`, `G49`), work offsets (`G54`..`G59`), and cycle return (`G98`, `G99`).\n- Parse `I`/`J`/`K` arcs and `R` radius arcs (`R > 0` minor arc, `R < 0` major arc) in XY, XZ, and YZ planes.\n- Expand canned cycles (`G73`, `G81`, `G82`, `G83`, `G84`, `G86`, `G89`) into explicit `cl::Move` chains (`crates/sim/src/sim.rs`).\n- Handle `T`, `M6`, `S`, `M3`/`M4`/`M5`, `M0`/`M1`/`M2`/`M30`, `G4`, `G61`/`G64`, and `G53`/`G28`/`G30` when reference positions exist.\n- Split sections on tool changes and record a 1-based source line number for every move.\n- Refuse unknown words, missing unit mode, `G41`/`G42`, macros (`G65`, `M98`, `#`), probing (`G31`, `G38.2`), `R` full circles, and `A`/`B`/`C` words by name with the 1-based line number.\n- Add a clean-room provenance comment to each module (`AGENTS.md`).\n\nDone means: `camcraft-gcode` builds in the workspace with a `docs/decisions/` entry, parses 3-axis ISO programs into `cl::Toolpath` sections with a 1-based line map, and tests pin modal tracking, `I`/`J`/`K` and `R` arcs, canned cycles, unit scaling, and named line-numbered refusals.\n\nPart of #2213\n",
